{%- comment -%}
  ==========================================================
  ARCHIVEOS — THE PRESERVATION SANCTUM
  RUUD BOY ARCHIVES

  The architectural room the archive stands in. Built from seven
  registered production PNG layers (1536×1024, same canvas) — this
  section composites them; it does not draw anything. The Archive
  Seal / RB-001 plaque is already rendered into the back-wall plate
  and is not recreated here.

  STATUS: master hero. This is the first viewport of the homepage
  (see templates/index.json, "hero" entry). The seven environment
  layers below are untouched from the structural-milestone version —
  only a content layer, a focal-point spotlight and viewport sizing
  have been added on top, all scoped under .archive-sanctum-hero so
  the plain environment (.archive-sanctum on its own) still composes
  the same way anywhere else it might be placed. Does not touch
  playback beyond reading the existing archive:trackchange /
  archive:play / archive:pause events archive-player.js already
  emits.

  Files:
    sections/archive-sanctum.liquid
    assets/archive-sanctum.css
    assets/archive-sanctum.js
  ==========================================================
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- comment -%} Self-contained: loads only on pages where this section is actually placed, not sitewide via snippets/stylesheets.liquid. {%- endcomment -%}
{{ 'archive-sanctum.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
<script src="{{ 'archive-sanctum.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>

<section class="archive-sanctum-hero" data-sanctum-hero aria-label="{{ shop.name }}">
  <div class="archive-sanctum" data-sanctum aria-hidden="true">
    <div class="archive-sanctum__frame">
      <img
        class="archive-sanctum__layer archive-sanctum__layer--wall"
        src="{{ 'sanctum-back-wall.png' | asset_url }}"
        width="1536"
        height="1024"
        alt=""
        loading="eager"
        fetchpriority="high"
      >
      <img
        class="archive-sanctum__layer archive-sanctum__layer--columns"
        src="{{ 'sanctum-columns.png' | asset_url }}"
        width="1536"
        height="1024"
        alt=""
        loading="eager"
      >
      <img
        class="archive-sanctum__layer archive-sanctum__layer--floor"
        src="{{ 'sanctum-memory-floor.png' | asset_url }}"
        width="1536"
        height="1024"
        alt=""
        loading="eager"
      >
      <img
        class="archive-sanctum__layer archive-sanctum__layer--light-shafts"
        src="{{ 'sanctum-atmosphere-light-shafts.png' | asset_url }}"
        width="1536"
        height="1024"
        alt=""
        loading="lazy"
      >
      <img
        class="archive-sanctum__layer archive-sanctum__layer--haze"
        src="{{ 'sanctum-atmosphere-haze.png' | asset_url }}"
        width="1536"
        height="1024"
        alt=""
        loading="lazy"
      >
      <img
        class="archive-sanctum__layer archive-sanctum__layer--dust"
        src="{{ 'sanctum-atmosphere-dust.png' | asset_url }}"
        width="1536"
        height="1024"
        alt=""
        loading="lazy"
      >
      <img
        class="archive-sanctum__layer archive-sanctum__layer--particles"
        src="{{ 'sanctum-atmosphere-particles.png' | asset_url }}"
        width="1536"
        height="1024"
        alt=""
        loading="lazy"
      >
    </div>
  </div>

  {%- comment -%}
    Light, not object: the crest is lit as the room's emblem, a
    faint beam falls from the ceiling onto the platform, and the
    platform itself pools the brightest — a stage, not a fabricated
    RB-001 object layer. Purely decorative — sits between the
    environment and the content layer.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <div class="archive-sanctum-hero__spotlight" aria-hidden="true"></div>

  {%- comment -%}
    A plain cinematic vignette (edges recede, centre column stays
    brightest) — not hiding anything. The wordmark below is small
    and sits above the crest rather than over it, so the crest's own
    engraving is meant to read clearly again.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <div class="archive-sanctum-hero__scrim" aria-hidden="true"></div>

  <div class="archive-sanctum-hero__content">
    {%- comment -%}
      No foreground heading here on purpose. The wall plate beneath
      the crest already carries "RUUD BOY ARCHIVES / PRESERVE. HONOR.
      SHARE. / RB-001" as a physical engraving — that IS the identity
      in this room. Duplicating it as HTML on top read as a webpage
      graphic laid over a photo, not an architectural space.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="archive-sanctum-hero__masthead">
      {%- if section.settings.tagline != blank -%}
        <p class="archive-sanctum-hero__tagline">{{ section.settings.tagline }}</p>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>

    <div class="archive-sanctum-hero__foot">
      {%- if section.settings.artifact_label != blank -%}
        <p class="archive-sanctum-hero__artifact">
          <span class="archive-sanctum-hero__artifact-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>{{ section.settings.artifact_label }}
        </p>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- if section.settings.cta_label != blank -%}
        <a class="archive-button archive-sanctum-hero__cta" href="{{ section.settings.cta_link }}">
          {{ section.settings.cta_label }}
        </a>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Sanctum",
  "tag": "section",
  "class": "section-archive-sanctum",
  "settings": [
    { "type": "header", "content": "Hero content" },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "tagline",
      "label": "Tagline",
      "default": "PRESERVE. HONOR. SHARE.",
      "info": "Leave empty to hide."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "artifact_label",
      "label": "Artifact label",
      "default": "RB-001",
      "info": "Leave empty to hide."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "cta_label",
      "label": "Button label",
      "default": "ENTER ARCHIVE",
      "info": "Leave empty to hide the button."
    },
    {
      "type": "url",
      "id": "cta_link",
      "label": "Button link"
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "Sanctum"
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
